            {
                "entry_id": "d915835f-2031-345b-b1db-e1e4a6475fdb",
                "word": "dilated",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "635205b5-ec6f-49e8-931c-612d4397e02a",
                        "entry_id": "d915835f-2031-345b-b1db-e1e4a6475fdb",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more dilated"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2e2eb172-6c07-4ea0-a9f2-5f214c3bd51b",
                        "entry_id": "d915835f-2031-345b-b1db-e1e4a6475fdb",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most dilated"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a834954-63dd-369b-bb5b-b280df7b546e",
                        "entry_id": "d915835f-2031-345b-b1db-e1e4a6475fdb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having undergone dilation; enlarged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4c977f7-2682-4a2c-94a5-a4061c1ddbd8",
                                "sense_id": "8a834954-63dd-369b-bb5b-b280df7b546e",
                                "text": "Now the rays of yellow being more refracted by the first Superficies of the said Air than those of red, are thereby made more oblique to the second Superficies, at which they are reflected to produce the colour'd Rings, and consequently the yellow Circle in each Ring will be more dilated than the red; and the Excess of its Dilatation will be so much the greater, by how much the greater is the obliquity of the Rays, until at last it become of equal extent with the red of the same Ring."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8247521f-b0d2-456b-9eb8-157eec7319c8",
                                "sense_id": "8a834954-63dd-369b-bb5b-b280df7b546e",
                                "text": "Is a little better, more conscious, and quieter, bowels purged, mercurial stools, pulse jerking 144, right pupil rather more dilated than the left."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9a95fda-b1ed-4848-8ebe-e3c29ecac6a3",
                                "sense_id": "8a834954-63dd-369b-bb5b-b280df7b546e",
                                "text": "Both pupils were very dilated, and quite inactive, excepting that she could distinguish light from darkness with the RIGHT eye, was quite blind, and had lost all power of smell."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "64af84ed-c987-4b3d-8dd2-4a605781e72f",
                                "sense_id": "8a834954-63dd-369b-bb5b-b280df7b546e",
                                "text": "M. Wecker found with ophthalmoscope a pale papilla, indications of hypertrophy of cellular tissue, very dilated veins, and some little hæmorrhagic spots."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79b4632d-d2ee-3f6e-a3d8-e893507cd37d",
                        "entry_id": "d915835f-2031-345b-b1db-e1e4a6475fdb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatively large."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fde79bca-b4d2-4816-91af-cc1503453e2e",
                                "sense_id": "79b4632d-d2ee-3f6e-a3d8-e893507cd37d",
                                "text": "The sternum forms a long, linear, deeply channeled lobe, between the coxæ, the apex very dilated, cordate, with a very elevated ridge in the centre, like a nose in profile"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89bf9f28-23f7-41de-b4a3-73b764f5ea11",
                                "sense_id": "79b4632d-d2ee-3f6e-a3d8-e893507cd37d",
                                "text": "Of the same form as C. 12-guttata, but having the elytra of the female more dilated, and the apical serratures and the sutural spine much more distinct."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26fe03b5-d23e-4bd4-98af-ed3c95deab6c",
                                "sense_id": "79b4632d-d2ee-3f6e-a3d8-e893507cd37d",
                                "text": "A species very easily distinguished from the others by its very dilated black wings, which have only a few marginal hyaline spots and very few discal subhyaline dots."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
